From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luisyr <106528106+luisyr1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: google: aoc: alsa: treat the zumapro AoC like zuma's for
 the pre-start data

The Pixel 9 Pro XL (zumapro, AoC firmware 16099865-polygon) shows the
same behaviour as the Pixel 8 Pro on the deep-buffer entry point EP6:
at the start its read index jumps to the write index and no interrupt
is raised. With aplay's default start threshold (the whole buffer)
the ALSA buffer stays full, hw_ptr stays at 0 and the write times out
with -EIO; with a small start threshold it plays.

Measured with ring_debug=1 on komodo, start threshold = buffer:
  prepared: written 4194304 read 4194304
  started:  written 4290304 read 4290304   (96000 bytes dropped)
  stopping: written 4290304 read 4290304   (5.4 s later, nothing read)

The previous patch only sets the flag for "google,zuma-aoc"; zumapro's
node is "google,zumapro-aoc", so match both.

Signed-off-by: Luisyr <106528106+luisyr1@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/google/aoc/alsa/aoc_alsa_card.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/google/aoc/alsa/aoc_alsa_card.c
@@ -2001,6 +2001,13 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* AoC firmware whose deep-buffer entry point drops the data written before the start */
+static const struct of_device_id aoc_drops_prefill_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "google,zuma-aoc" },
+	{ .compatible = "google,zumapro-aoc" },
+	{ }
+};
+
 static int snd_aoc_init(struct aoc_chip *chip)
 {
 	int i;
@@ -2070,8 +2077,11 @@
 
 	of_node_put(aoc_node);
 
-	/* Only the zuma AoC firmware drops the pre-start playback data; gs201 is left as it was. */
-	aoc_node = of_find_compatible_node(NULL, NULL, "google,zuma-aoc");
+	/*
+	 * Only the zuma and zumapro AoC firmware drops the pre-start playback
+	 * data; gs201 is left as it was.
+	 */
+	aoc_node = of_find_matching_node(NULL, aoc_drops_prefill_match);
 	chip->deep_buffer_drops_prefill = !!aoc_node;
 	of_node_put(aoc_node);
 	return 0;
